# Keep Cursor docs current

After meaningful product, schema, API, or layout changes, update the docs in the **same session** (or at the next natural pause). Do not wait for the user to ask again.

## Keep in sync

- `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`
- `README.md` — the first file a new operator reads, and the one that goes stale unnoticed
- `.cursor/README.md`
- **Every** file under `.cursor/rules/` — a glob-scoped rule fires on files whose subsystem may have moved, so `stack`, `admin-ownership`, `studio-generation`, `brand-theme` and `skills-availability` count as much as the always-on ones
- **Every** file under `docs/`

Removing a subsystem is not done until the doc set has been grepped for its name. `tests/unit/docs-accuracy.test.ts` mechanises the part of this that can be: coverage floors, the verify step list, setting keys, env vars, stack prompts, worktree ports, the runner every documented repo script is invoked through, and the banned `npm` / `yarn` / `pnpm exec` command forms are all read out of the source and compared. It cannot check prose, which is why this rule still exists.

## Lessons-learned lifecycle

`.cursor/lessons-learned.md` is the one doc that is also an instruction file — this file and the always-on `self-evolving-memory` rule both tell every agent to read it before starting. So a stale entry there does not just misinform a reader, it instructs the next agent to preserve infrastructure that is gone. Deleting a subsystem includes grepping that file for its name.

Entries are **never deleted** (a deleted lesson gets re-learned). Append exactly one marker bullet as the entry's last bullet and leave its original three untouched:

- `- **Superseded [YYYY-MM-DD]:** …` — the rule still binds, only its example moved; point at the live equivalent.
- `- **Obsolete [YYYY-MM-DD]:** …` — the mistake is unreachable because its subsystem is gone; say what deleted it and what still generalises.

Either marker must name a replacement, and an unmarked entry is a live instruction — never mark one whose subject is still in the tree. `tests/unit/lessons-learned-lifecycle.test.ts` checks the marker shape, that no entry lost its bullets, and that the subjects existing markers call dead really are still absent.

## Rules

- Reflect what actually exists. Do not invent features.
- Merge short deltas. Do not rewrite whole guides.
- Do not dump `omni-*` / `gstack-*` / Coolify / WHM skill trees into this repo.
- Do not commit unless asked. Never write secrets.

```text
# ❌ BAD — ship a new API and leave the map stale
add /api/projects/[id]/plan, skip AGENTS.md

# ✅ GOOD — same session
add the route, then note Plan/Build in AGENTS.md / .cursor/README.md
```
